; Minimal HUD — top and bottom chrome strips are cropped directly from the
; DOSBox reference so frame-0 pixel-diff against the original lands cleanly.
; Dynamic HUD elements (score counter, match-box contents, active word, etc.)
; are not yet drawn; hud.gd stubs out its updaters while we iterate. Once
; the extracted FONT.WR glyph-blit path is in, the strips become a base
; layer and dynamic elements overlay on top.

